# libbox64dl explicit plugin set. Copy to plugins.conf (or pass as
# PLUGIN_CONFIG=<path>) to make the *set of grafted plugin directories* explicit.
#
# One `name = path` line per plugin. `path` is the plugin directory, absolute or
# relative to the libbox64dl repo root, and must contain library_list.inc,
# wrapped<lib>.c and wrapped<lib>_private.h. Blank lines and `#` comments are
# ignored; paths must not contain spaces.
#
# SCOPE -- what this does and does not pin:
#   * It pins WHICH directories are grafted and where they resolve to. It
#     deliberately does not restrict dynamic-symbol visibility: the wrapped
#     library tables keep exporting the `my_*` / wrapper symbols box64's dlsym
#     path may look up.
#   * It pins a LOCATION, not a version. A path carries no commit, tag or file
#     hash of the plugin sources, so a sibling checkout can change under the same
#     path. Content-level reproducibility needs the plugin's own revision pinned
#     (and, ideally, hashes recorded) -- that is outside this file.
#   * Without plugins.conf the build grafts every plugins/<name>/ entry, which
#     keeps the developer symlink workflow working -- including absolute symlinks
#     into a sibling checkout, e.g. uninode's:
#
#       plugins/libnode -> /home/<user>/.../uninode/wrapped
#
#     That default set is untracked and machine-specific; this example does not
#     fix it, and no release build should claim full reproducibility from it
#     until the plugin sources themselves are pinned.
#
# Generate this file from the currently resolved set, then review and commit it:
#
#   make -C libbox64dl plugin-manifest > plugins.conf
#
# `make -C libbox64dl check-plugins` validates the set and warns about plugin
# directories that resolve outside this repository.
#
# libgccs is the in-repo plugin; keep it in any explicit manifest or wine's
# libgcc unwinding symbols are gone.
libgccs = plugins/libgccs

# A downstream plugin resolved through its checkout, pinned by path (location
# only, not a version):
# libnode = ../uninode/wrapped
